From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:33:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Keep the object stores' rows in the database actor

Every request read the row of its object store and the store's indexes
(queries::object_store, a LEFT JOIN with ORDER BY) before it ran. RDB
prepares every statement anew, and on the DAYU200 that read took 41 % of
the database actor's cycles in a profile of puts and cursor steps, more
than the cursor step's own statement.

The actor now keeps the rows that requests read (Database::stores), as
its connection sees them: inside the open SQL transaction, or as of the
last commit, which is what the transactions that the scheduler lets run
alongside see. A put updates the key generator's current number in the
row along with the database. Every rollback (abort, a failed write, a
failed commit, an SQL transaction that ended on its own) and every schema
operation other than a population step drops the rows; schema operations
read and write the tables themselves. Tests that change the database
through the test connection drop them too.

Validation: `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` (host SQLite): 142 passed, 1 skipped; test_requests_read_a_store_row_once fails when a request reads the row again (checked by re-reading it in object_store); `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets --no-default-features --features ohos-rdb-backend` and `cargo clippy -p servo-storage --lib -- -D warnings`: no warnings. DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, checked-release), temporary probe page of 2,000 records each, this commit alone vs the previous one: store cursor 1.71 -> 1.08 ms per step, index cursor 1.93 -> 1.25 ms, puts 1,128 -> 1,805/s without an index, 714 -> 933/s with a unique index, 2,000 cursor.update()+continue() 5.07 -> 4.25 s. The WPT runs of the series are in the last commit of the series (P4.2).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; profiled puts and cursor steps on the board with hiperf, kept the rows in the actor, added the backend test, measured on host and board)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
